1
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,720
Did you do it on purpose

2
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,840
last time?

3
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:47,320
Which time?

4
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:51,480
The time your mouth

5
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:55,160
attacked mine.

6
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:58,680
Last time

7
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:00,340
was truly an accident.

8
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:05,239
But this time, it can be on purpose.

9
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:19,960
Finally reached the top.

10
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:23,720
Shen Feng!

11
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,880
Last time I climbed all the way up here

12
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,000
and saw nothing.

13
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:41,320
Driving up this time,
I actually saw a sunshower.

14
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:43,160
Sure enough,
choice matters more than effort.

15
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:44,680
Shortcuts are the real deal.

16
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:46,410
Some things are just like that.

17
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,360
The harder you chase them,

18
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,860
the further away they get.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,240
But sometimes,

20
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,039
if you let go,

21
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,360
maybe one day,

22
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,240
when you suddenly look back,

23
00:01:57,479 --> 00:01:58,740
it's right behind you.

24
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,480
I've always wanted to ask you.

25
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:04,800
You're so good at math,

26
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:06,160
why did you give it up

27
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,220
and come back here?

28
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,760
Math used to be my obsession.

29
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:14,920
It brought me
the highest sense of achievement

30
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,360
and the purest joy.

31
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,740
But until one day I suddenly realized

32
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,360
my abilities

33
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:23,480
seemed to end there,

34
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:25,380
which made me very miserable.

35
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,240
Until I met you.

36
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,720
You told me

37
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,400
that persistence is valuable,

38
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,460
but giving up isn't shameful either.

39
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:36,480
So,

40
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,440
I tried to change my mindset,

41
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,170
accepting my successes

42
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,640
and my failures.

43
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,600
There isn't just one path in life.

44
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,000
So I took a different one.

45
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,760
I'm very satisfied with my life now.

46
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:54,880
Just because of that one thing I said?

47
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,040
At that time,

48
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:00,640
I just wanted you
to keep playing games with me.

49
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,160
China lost a Gauss because of me.

50
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:05,880
I'm a terrible sinner.

51
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:06,560
My bad.

52
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,160
Don't flatter me.

53
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,240
I know where my limits are.

54
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:18,480
I don't really have any grand ambitions.

55
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:20,079
And I don't know what kind of life

56
00:03:20,079 --> 00:03:20,680
I'd like.

57
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:22,900
That's perfectly normal.

58
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,920
Actually,
feeling lost is the norm in life.

59
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,730
Some people might find
their direction quickly,

60
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,800
but some spend their whole lives

61
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,400
figuring it out.

62
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,960
But even if you never find it,

63
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,520
you still have to love yourself well.

64
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,520
Eat well, sleep well,

65
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,850
and live every day well.

66
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:44,880
You don't have to
deliberately search for the answer.

67
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:47,640
Maybe one day the answer will come to you.

68
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:49,770
It's so beautiful here.

69
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:50,880
I took pictures everywhere,

70
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:51,960
my storage is full.

71
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,079
It's a pity I have work tomorrow,

72
00:03:56,079 --> 00:03:58,280
so I have to leave today.

73
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,360
That's okay,

74
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,780
you're welcome to visit again next time.

75
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:03,360
Let's take a group photo then.

76
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:08,640
To commemorate the three of us
here and now.

77
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,280
Sure, come on.

78
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:10,960
Let's go.

79
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:17,920
Three, two, one.

80
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,930
Stayed up all night yesterday,

81
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,600
and stared at the sun all morning today.

82
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,480
My eyes hurt so much.

83
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:44,880
Lutein.

84
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:48,400
Our eyes like you.

85
00:04:51,159 --> 00:04:52,760
This worked out pretty well.

86
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,000
We're getting more and more bookings.

87
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,800
Let me see
who the next experience officer is...

88
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:01,680
Welcome!

89
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:05,000
We're here for the event.

90
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,900
Okay, please show me your IDs.

91
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:09,520
Thank you.

92
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,480
You two did indeed win our event.

93
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:16,320
But the registration info says

94
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:19,120
it's for a man and a woman.

95
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,800
That person couldn't make it.

96
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:22,460
Can't we just swap someone in?

97
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,600
Sure, why not?

98
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,600
Here are your room cards.

99
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,640
You two go check in first,

100
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,370
and I'll show you around later.

101
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:36,440
No need.

102
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:38,080
We're not participating in any activities.

103
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,680
But that activity is really great.

104
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,400
I said no.

105
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,960
Are you forcing us to try it?

106
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,240
No.

107
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:46,400
We just want to sleep,

108
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:47,280
get it?

109
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,240
Let me tell you,

110
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,159
stop bothering us,

111
00:05:49,159 --> 00:05:50,960
or else we'll leave a bad review.

112
00:05:52,159 --> 00:05:54,440
All right. Sweet dreams, you two.

113
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:55,960
This way, please.

114
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:58,760
Your ID cards.

115
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,120
Easy,

116
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:18,920
easy.

117
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,600
Here we go. Careful.

118
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:30,580
Isn't this the mattress from our B&B?

119
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,200
What are you doing?

120
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:34,800
Are you okay?

121
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:37,560
Hair dryer, teapot...

122
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:39,800
What are you doing?

123
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:40,880
Are you moving out?

124
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,800
Why don't you just tear down my B&B?

125
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,920
We booked the room.

126
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:45,920
These are ours.

127
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:46,960
Why can't we take them?

128
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:47,560
Exactly.

129
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:50,080
You did get a free trial,

130
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,480
but even if you paid for the stay,

131
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,640
you can't do this.

132
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:53,400
Just take a tea bag

133
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:54,960
and a pair of disposable slippers.

134
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,440
Isn't this just robbery?

135
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,040
Cut the crap.

136
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,700
Ignore her and get out of here.

137
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,480
These are our things.

138
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,640
Our things. Give it to me.

139
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:04,360
Don't take our things.

140
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,880
They are robbers.

141
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:12,610
They're emptying the homestay.
Call the police!

142
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,440
You dare call the police?

143
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,080
Shen Feng!

144
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:18,680
Bro!

145
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:22,060
I'm trained, I'm telling you.

146
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:30,880
Shen Feng!

147
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:32,880
Are you okay?

148
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:34,240
I'm fine.

149
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,280
What's wrong?

150
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:37,200
Those two are bandits.

151
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:38,200
They want to loot Yunbian.

152
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,000
Shut up!

153
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:40,540
How dare you call for help!

154
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:42,200
Shanchuan!

155
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,480
Shanchuan!

156
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,130
Are you alright?

157
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,080
Don't ever let me see you again.

158
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:01,610
Get lost!

159
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,520
Nice!

160
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:06,960
That's amazing.

161
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,440
Good thing only the protector cracked,

162
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:16,600
not the screen.

163
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:20,840
Are you sure you can do this?

164
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:21,440
If not,

165
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:23,720
I'll go to the city tomorrow
to get a new one.

166
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,160
Just leave it to me.

167
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,560
My skills

168
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:29,160
are way better than
those 20-yuan quick fixes on the street.

169
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:31,360
Watch me restore it to its former glory.

170
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:37,260
There are weirdos every year,

171
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,559
but seeing someone

172
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:40,600
empty out everything at Yunbian like today

173
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:41,760
is a first for me.

174
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,720
Good thing you showed up in time.

175
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:45,160
I couldn't tell,

176
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,450
but you're actually pretty tough.

177
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:50,460
How am I fierce?

178
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,640
Fierce in a fight.

179
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:54,880
You calmly took on two guys,

180
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,840
charging into them with your huge fists

181
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,640
and fighting your way in and out.

182
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:01,040
I must make a solemn declaration
about this.

183
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,640
Though I'm happy you're praising me,

184
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:04,040
they threw the first punch.

185
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:05,560
It was self-defense.

186
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:06,840
Got it.

187
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,440
Righteous protagonists

188
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:10,330
never cross the line of the law.

189
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,280
Right?

190
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:19,600
Why are there so many bubbles on this?

191
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,240
That's because the screen protector
you bought is too cheap.

192
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,240
I told you

193
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:25,300
to buy one that costs at least 15 yuan.

194
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:26,200
Are you sure

195
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,080
it's not because

196
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:30,240
you kept blabbering

197
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:31,570
and blew all the dust in?

198
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:38,760
A message from Jia.

199
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,220
I didn't see anything.

200
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:43,520
Jia and I are just friends.

201
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:45,040
It's not what you think.

202
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:46,680
Who asked?

203
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,000
Fine,

204
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:50,580
you didn't ask.
I just wanted to say it, okay?

205
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,240
Why are you here?

206
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,500
To bring you medicine.

207
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,160
How's your hand?

208
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:18,640
It's just a scratch. I'm fine.

209
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:23,040
A scratch?

210
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,200
It's bruised.

211
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:26,200
Do I have to take you to the hospital?

212
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,130
Did you hurt your waist too?

213
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,440
I went to the hospital.

214
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,900
The doctor said it's fine.

215
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,400
Come here.

216
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:41,300
Let me apply the medicine for you.

217
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,880
I'd better do it myself.

218
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,440
Turn around

219
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:36,800
and lift your shirt.
